+# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
+# [MP8] 8-player seating (2026-08-17)
+# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
+#
+# **Layout decision B** (measured with probe48/49, not guessed) — **the 4 vanilla seats are not changed by a single byte**,
+# and 2 new seats are inserted on each side, at z = **+0.28** (between two vanilla seats) and **-2.15** (the gap at the table's -z end).
+#
+# ⚠️ **"Extend the table and add seats" is blocked in both directions** (that was the original plan ①, rejected after testing).
+#   * **+z direction** — the camera sits at (0, 4.26, 4.31) **looking toward -z**, and the tabletop already reaches z=2.86,
+#     only 1.45 m from the lens — adding people on this side would smear them right across the camera.
+#     (Candidate C in testing — the pair at z=2.20 lands at ±0.93 on screen, hugging the edge, and the chairs also stick 2 cm past the tabletop.)
+#   * **-z direction** — the coach's chair occupies z[-4.83, -3.33] and the tabletop reaches -2.86, leaving only 0.47 m in between.
+#
+# ⚠️ **Why not "4 seats evenly spaced per side"** (candidate A, where 1.43 spacing just fits 4 chairs)?
+#   Doing that **moves the vanilla seats**, and the coach's shooting animations are **hand-made per seat**
+#   (`coach_shoot_position_0..3`, only these 4 exist in the whole table) — once the seats move,
+#   the 4 that used to aim correctly all go off as well. Keeping vanilla = 4 of the 8 seats with perfect aim.
+#
+# Screen projection check (pitfall #25, all inside the frame, farthest ±0.70, the same as the farthest vanilla seat)
+#     z=-2.15 → ±0.36    z=-0.73 → ±0.45    z=+0.28 → ±0.54    z=+1.29 → ±0.70
+#
+# The cost is that the chair at z=+0.28 **overlaps each neighbor on the left and right by 0.34 m**
+# (on 2026-08-17 the user explicitly allowed "overlap when necessary").
+const MP8_NEW_SEAT_Z: Array[float] = [0.28, -2.15]
+
+# network_manager reads this flag via Object.get(), and when it reads true it leaves our spawn point container alone.
+# ⚠️ **This is required**. This container's name `PlayerSpawnPositions` is on the whitelist for generic slot filling,
+#    and the generic algorithm takes "the midpoint of the line between adjacent points" — which would put the new seats **right in the middle of the table**.
+var mp8_owns_spawns: bool = true
+
+var _mp8_seat_z: Array[float] = []      # index = seat number, value = that seat's world z
+
+# [MP8] The order in which players were shot by the coach. Vanilla only erases them from active_players and doesn't record the order,
+# but placement scoring needs to rank the people who didn't finish eating — dying later beats dying earlier (they dodged longer).
+# This is the only new order array added here. Finish order uses vanilla's existing finished_players,
+# and reaching halfway uses vanilla's existing halfway_done_players (per user rule 2, use the existing order arrays).
+var _mp8_dead_order: Array[int] = []
+
